!!id:"https://tson.io/test-suite/class2/schema/valid/a-reference-writes-its-of-alone-expected.tn"
!!import:"https://tson.io/test-suite/schemas/schema-sidecar.tn"
{
  spec: "[TSON-SCHEMA] §4.2, [TSON-SCHEMA] §8.1"
  description: """
    A reference's resolved form is `of` alone. The names it admits -- here the entries whose value is of
    `uuid_type`, the two ids and not `count` -- are the linker's judgement over the closure of the schema that
    links it, derived and never written, so nothing beside `of` is a fact of the body. A reference is a set of
    names and carries no `disjoint`: that is a sum's fact.
    """
  valid: {
    resolved: """
      !schema {
        stock_id => !uuid_type {}

        customer_id => !uuid_type {}

        count => !integer_type {}

        any_id => !reference { of: uuid_type }
      }
      """
  }
}
